2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And no matter the size from twin to king, it's the same price. And we also have today matching duvet sets if you're in the market for a duvet. So, with our deal, these are $47.50.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PEACHSKINSHEETS, 50% OFF\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, really size does not matter. Okay.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. Okay. So, this is Jill & Ally, they are mother/daughter duo.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sort of reality TV stars that want to bring a little joy to everybody's home. So, we've got pillows, blankets, candles, mugs. I chose this one for you. This is the one I would give to you.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ooh, #blessed.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There you go.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible)\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oversized mug. I also really love these manifestation candles.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look at how beautiful that is.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Incredible.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it comes with this crystal inside that you can keep the crystal obviously once the candle has burned. And they just have really pretty messaging on it and it's a nice sturdy fabulous candle. Everything from this line is spectacular. And really good prices that start at $6.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JILL & ALLY, 51% - 76% OFF\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cha-ching. We're all about manifesting.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, exactly. Exactly. And then finally, in this round of "Deals," we've got Butter London. We've got a huge assortment.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All of their clean and luxurious skin care, brushes too this time, so polishes, makeup. What I love also about their makeup, we were all just talking about it, is they have options that you can go with that like no makeup-makeup look or full on glam.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They've got you covered. I love their lip products. You can't go wrong with anything from this brand. All fan favorites and these, too, start at $6.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUTTER LONDON, 50% - 66% OFF\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such good deals. Love that the brushes are included today, too.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All of these deals are on our website, goodmorningamerica.com. Tory is sticking around, treating us with another round of "Deals & Steals." So, get ready for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220823ei860000q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INDIANA PASSES NEW ABORTION BAN FIRST STATE POST-ROE TO APPROVE NEAR-TOTAL BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DEATH VALLEY NATIONAL PARK, FLOODING, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALIFORNIA FLOODING STRANDS HUNDREDS\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , MARLOW, SHOOTING, DEATHS, PORTER\par \par \uc2 BILL, CLIMATE CHANGE, SENATE, DEBATE, MARKEY, WARREN, SCHATZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR CLIMATE PACKAGE MOVES FORWARD\par \par \uc2 INDIANA, ABORTION, BAN, ROE V. WADE, GLICK, BERNARD, JACOB\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the battle over abortion, Indiana passing a near total ban on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The state's Republican-controlled legislature becoming the first in the nation to pass such a measure, following the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade. There are some exceptions, but opponents, including the White House, are blasting the legislation. Here's ABC's Faith Abubey.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DEVELOPMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INDIANA PASSES NEW ABORTION BAN: FIRST STATE POST-ROE TO APPROVE NEAR-TOTAL BAN\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Indiana now the first state to approve a near-total abortion ban since the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLICK (REP) (INDIANA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 We have heard from a number of individuals who are saying protect these children, protect life.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Republican governor \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2  signing the ban into law late Friday night. Former Vice President and Indiana native \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  tweeting, quote, "Life is winning!" Currently, Indiana law allows abortions for up to 22 weeks of pregnancy. Under the new legislation, all abortions would be banned, except in cases of fatal abnormalities in the fetus, when a mother's health is at risk and some instances of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 DR. CAITLIN BERNARD (INDIANA OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 This is going to be very, very restrictive, and it's going to hurt Hoosier women.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Caitlin Bernard entering the national debate when she performed an abortion on a 10-year-old rape victim who traveled to Indiana after the procedure became illegal in her home state of Ohio. Indiana now joining at least 15 states at have ceased nearly all abortion services, those states having previous laws on the books before the Supreme Court decision. Indiana's Republican-controlled state legislature passed the bill. However, some Republicans still say it doesn't go far enough.\par \par \uc2 REP. JOHN JACOB (REP) (INDIANA)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is always murder.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "...ANOTHER RADICAL STEP BY REPUBLICAN LEGISLATORS TO TAKE AWAY WOMEN'S REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS..."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE WHITE HOUSE STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The White House today blasting the legislation as, quote, "another radical step by Republican legislators to take away women's reproductive rights."\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Our bodies.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Our choice.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Indiana's near-total abortion ban comes after an overwhelming majority of voters just last week defeated an effort to remove abortion rights from the Kansas state constitution.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Faith Abubey is back with us, now. And Faith, like we saw in Kansas, there, Democrats in Indiana were also hoping that their voters could weigh in on whether abortion should remain legal in the state. So, what happened, there?\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, Indiana Democrats were you pushing to get the nonbinding abortion question on the November ballot. However, that measure failed. The near-total abortion ban goes into effect September 15th. Whit?\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020220808ei8600005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FALLOUT AFTER SURPRISE KANSAS ABORTION VOTE PRESIDENT BIDEN SIGNS EXECUTIVE ORDER ON ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HEAT, RECORD, ADVISORIES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ABORTION, KANSAS, VOTE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Robin. We're going to get the latest now on the battle over abortion. President Biden signed an executive order on abortion access and called out Kansas for that decisive vote protecting abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The voters of Kansas sent a powerful signal that this fall the American people will vote to preserve and protect the right and refuse to let them be ripped away by politicians and my administration has their back.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Chief White House correspondent Cecilia Vega joins us now. Good morning, Cecilia.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT DOES IT MEAN FOR THE MIDTERMS?\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning to you. So President Biden, and frankly the rest of his party, they are really looking at Kansas hoping that this is a sign of what's to come in just 96 days when voters head to the ballot box for these midterms. Look, you know this, Kansas is a deeply red state. Voters sent a clear message there to defend abortion rights, even in some of the most conservative leaning counties, and this was a surprise, this measure was defeated. So Democrats right now, they're really hoping that this issue galvanizes their base, especially when it comes to that coveted vote of suburban women. They're using this as part of this broader messaging campaign to paint Republicans as extremists on social issues, but Republicans, they are clear on this one. They say the midterms are going to end up being about a referendum on the President and the economy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION MEASURES ON BALLOT THIS YEAR\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Abortion really, the reality is, take a look at this, only on the ballot in four other states this year, so it really remains to be seen whether this is going to become one of these defining issues that gets voters to the polls. So the President, you mentioned there, he signed that EO yesterday aiming to help low income women who live in states where the procedure is banned to travel to other states. He is really, George, trying to show that his administration is out front on this one, but, frankly, when it comes to this eo they have offered very few details about how this is actually going to end up working or how, frankly, the government is going to be able to pay for this one.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Cecilia, the 2020 election lie and how elections will be administered in the future also on the ballot in November.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES PRIMARY FALLOUT: WHAT DO RESULTS MEAN FOR THE MIDTERMS?\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah and with that, George, frankly, that means President Trump is what we're talking about. He is really going to be a spotlight, this issue of the election lie. So look at this, four states nominating Republican candidates to roles overseeing elections in those states. They all, right now, back Trump's efforts to overturn that 2020 race, so we could potentially be talking, George, here about a very serious impact on voting for millions of Americans around this country.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Huge consequences. Cecilia Vega, thanks very much. Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220902ei8400003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BEHIND THE SCENES OF CMA FEST THE WORLD'S BIGGEST COUNTRY MUSIC EVENT RETURNS\b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS HELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES PRIMARY SHOWDOWNS\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, KANSAS, ABORTION, TURNOUT\par \par \uc2 PRIMARIES, RESULTS, GOP, TRUMP, CONTENTIOUS\par \par \uc2 CIPOLLONE, DOJ, SUBPOENAED, EASTMAN, PROBE\par \par \uc2 PELOSI, TAIWAN, CHINA, TENSIONS, DEMOCRACY\par \par \uc2 ALERT, STATE DEPT, AL-ZAWAHIRI, LUTE, DRONE\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, ALERT, TALIBAN, DOHA, PELOSI, CHINA\par \par \uc2 SCULLY, DODGERS, HALL OF FAME, LEGACY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT SPOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, SANCTIONS, SALAMA, KABAEVA, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 NFL, DOLPHINS, PENALIZED, BRADY, ROSS, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 CPSC\uc2 , RECALLED, T.J. MAXX, FINED, INFANT\par \par \uc2 PHILIP, PARACHUTE, TANGLED, FREEFALLING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 BASKETBALL, BLUE COLLAR U, BUFFALO\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, REFERENDUM, ELECTION, KANSAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS VOTES TO PROTECT ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTERS BLOCK AMENDMENT IN POST-ROE REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 MONKEYPOX, CHILDREN, MEDICINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING MONKEYPOX CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIFTH CHILD IN U.S. TESTS POSITIVE FOR VIRUS\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, KENTUCKY, WEATHER, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THREAT TO KENTUCKY FLOOD ZONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURVIVORS FACE DEVASTATION & DANGEROUS HEAT\par \par \uc2 LOVATO, SINGER, GENDER, IDENTITY, PRONOUNS, CRUZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMII LOVATO SPEAKS OUT ABOUT GENDER IDENTITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SINGER ADDED 'SHE/HER' PRONOUNS\par \par \uc2 DISORDERED EATING, CHILDREN, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN & DISORDERED EATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: KIDS AS YOUNG AS 9 ENGAGING IN BEHAVIOR\par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY, REFURBISHED, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO SCHOOL SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUYING REFURBISHED TECH TO CUT COSTS\par \par \uc2 STYLES, "ROAD HOUSE", NOSTALGIA\par \par \uc2 CMA, MUSIC, FESTIVAL, COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEHIND THE SCENES OF CMA FEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE WORLD'S BIGGEST COUNTRY MUSIC EVENT RETURNS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...biggest event in country music, the CMA Music Festival, returning for the first time since before the pandemic. Ashan Singh went behind the scenes.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the biggest country music event, and its return is more epic than ever. For the first time since 2019, the main stage at Nissan Stadium is flooded with the greats for the event for country music fans and stars can't get enough of.\par \par \uc2 CARLY PEARCE (SINGER)\par \par \uc2 It feels so just exciting to be back. I feel like it's something that makes country music and Nashville so special, and we've been missing it.\par \par \uc2 KELSEA BALLERINI (SINGER)\par \par \uc2 It's a city full of the people that love country music the most. You feel that connection. You feel that love in the air.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) CMA Fest, a four-day festival with thousands in the heart of music city, featuring 30 performances from some of country's hottest musicians.\par \par \uc2 KANE BROWN (SINGER)\par \par \uc2 I'm excited. You know, I haven't played Nashville since the last time, either, so I'm really excited to just bring the new energy that I found on stage.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For the past two years, the festival has been put on hold due to the COVID-19 pandemic. Now back, even the artists are feeling the jitters.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's going through your head? How are you feeling?\par \par \uc2 THOMAS RHETT (SINGER)\par \par \uc2 I feel good, man. I kind of forgot how to talk to crowds. I think when you're, when just with your, with your small family for a year, and all of a sudden you're looking at 20,000 people, you're like, hey.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And for many of the artists, the opportunity to be on the main stage, a dream come true.\par \par \uc2 LAINEY WILSON (SINGER)\par \par \uc2 I just wanted to be a part of the country music world, the industry. It took a lot longer than I wanted it to.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But that motivation to get on that main stage is what ultimately kept you going?\par \par \uc2 LAINEY WILSON (SINGER)\par \par \uc2 That's it. That's it.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And guys, make sure to check out the music event of the summer only tonight on ABC at 8:00, 7:00 Central. You know I'll be watching.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Me too.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are in. We're Thank you so much. Coming up, "GMA's" Dog Days of Summer live in Dallas. Come on back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220901ei830003i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS HELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES PRIMARY SHOWDOWNS\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, KANSAS, ABORTION, TURNOUT\par \par \uc2 PRIMARIES, RESULTS, GOP, TRUMP, CONTENTIOUS\par \par \uc2 CIPOLLONE, DOJ, SUBPOENAED, EASTMAN, PROBE\par \par \uc2 PELOSI, TAIWAN, CHINA, TENSIONS, DEMOCRACY\par \par \uc2 ALERT, STATE DEPT, AL-ZAWAHIRI, LUTE, DRONE\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, ALERT, TALIBAN, DOHA, PELOSI, CHINA\par \par \uc2 SCULLY, DODGERS, HALL OF FAME, LEGACY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT SPOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, SANCTIONS, SALAMA, KABAEVA, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 NFL, DOLPHINS, PENALIZED, BRADY, ROSS, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 CPSC\uc2 , RECALLED, T.J. MAXX, FINED, INFANT\par \par \uc2 PHILIP, PARACHUTE, TANGLED, FREEFALLING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 BASKETBALL, BLUE COLLAR U, BUFFALO\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, REFERENDUM, ELECTION, KANSAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS VOTES TO PROTECT ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTERS BLOCK AMENDMENT IN POST-ROE REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 MONKEYPOX, CHILDREN, MEDICINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING MONKEYPOX CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIFTH CHILD IN U.S. TESTS POSITIVE FOR VIRUS\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, KENTUCKY, WEATHER, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THREAT TO KENTUCKY FLOOD ZONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURVIVORS FACE DEVASTATION & DANGEROUS HEAT\par \par \uc2 LOVATO, SINGER, GENDER, IDENTITY, PRONOUNS, CRUZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMII LOVATO SPEAKS OUT ABOUT GENDER IDENTITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SINGER ADDED 'SHE/HER' PRONOUNS\par \par \uc2 DISORDERED EATING, CHILDREN, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN & DISORDERED EATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: KIDS AS YOUNG AS 9 ENGAGING IN BEHAVIOR\par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY, REFURBISHED, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO SCHOOL SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUYING REFURBISHED TECH TO CUT COSTS\par \par \uc2 STYLES, "ROAD HOUSE", NOSTALGIA\par \par \uc2 CMA, MUSIC, FESTIVAL, COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEHIND THE SCENES OF CMA FEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE WORLD'S BIGGEST COUNTRY MUSIC EVENT RETURNS\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 SERVICE DOG, BEST MAN, VETERAN, MORGAN\par \par \uc2 COOKING, GUARNASCHELLI, PICNIC, RECIPES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ginger, you're missing it, Ginger. We miss you, Ging. It's great.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOG DAYS OF SUMMER\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am missing it, but don't worry, I am in dog heaven. This is Renee's little sister. I can't stand it. If they keep bringing puppies with the saddest eyes and the happiest joy, I don't know what I'm going to do. But we thought why not share a dog forecast with all these newly adopted dogs, just to celebrate a little bit more. We brought out some cities with pictures of our dogs, the meteorology dogs of "Good Morning America." Dog Town, California, got a couple of thunderstorms possible. You know your pets are not going to love that. Labrador Hill, New York, sunny and 81. And look at Wolf Lake, Indiana. They're in that hot, hot head advisory.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTHEAST HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's the big picture. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oscar winner Ron Howard, he is here live in Times Square.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220901ei830003m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BACK TO SCHOOL SAVINGS BUYING REFURBISHED TECH TO CUT COSTS\b0\par\par\uc2 971 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS HELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES PRIMARY SHOWDOWNS\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, KANSAS, ABORTION, TURNOUT\par \par \uc2 PRIMARIES, RESULTS, GOP, TRUMP, CONTENTIOUS\par \par \uc2 CIPOLLONE, DOJ, SUBPOENAED, EASTMAN, PROBE\par \par \uc2 PELOSI, TAIWAN, CHINA, TENSIONS, DEMOCRACY\par \par \uc2 ALERT, STATE DEPT, AL-ZAWAHIRI, LUTE, DRONE\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, ALERT, TALIBAN, DOHA, PELOSI, CHINA\par \par \uc2 SCULLY, DODGERS, HALL OF FAME, LEGACY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT SPOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, SANCTIONS, SALAMA, KABAEVA, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 NFL, DOLPHINS, PENALIZED, BRADY, ROSS, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 CPSC\uc2 , RECALLED, T.J. MAXX, FINED, INFANT\par \par \uc2 PHILIP, PARACHUTE, TANGLED, FREEFALLING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 BASKETBALL, BLUE COLLAR U, BUFFALO\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, REFERENDUM, ELECTION, KANSAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS VOTES TO PROTECT ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTERS BLOCK AMENDMENT IN POST-ROE REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 MONKEYPOX, CHILDREN, MEDICINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING MONKEYPOX CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIFTH CHILD IN U.S. TESTS POSITIVE FOR VIRUS\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, KENTUCKY, WEATHER, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THREAT TO KENTUCKY FLOOD ZONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURVIVORS FACE DEVASTATION & DANGEROUS HEAT\par \par \uc2 LOVATO, SINGER, GENDER, IDENTITY, PRONOUNS, CRUZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMII LOVATO SPEAKS OUT ABOUT GENDER IDENTITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SINGER ADDED 'SHE/HER' PRONOUNS\par \par \uc2 DISORDERED EATING, CHILDREN, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN & DISORDERED EATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: KIDS AS YOUNG AS 9 ENGAGING IN BEHAVIOR\par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY, REFURBISHED, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO SCHOOL SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUYING REFURBISHED TECH TO CUT COSTS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Robin. Now it's time to turn to our Inflation Nation series. As parents start making back-to-school purchases, of course, our Becky Worley is here to teach a lesson on buying refurbished tech for teens. And Becky, you brought, you brought some A-plus students with you.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, A-plus are they? Well, I don't know about that, but these are my kids, Finn and Emmy, who practically grew up on "GMA." You guys, how many segments do you think you've been on?\par \par \uc2 EMALIA WORLEY (DAUGHTER OF BECKY WORLEY)\par \par \uc2 Probably 40.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Forty?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He probably filmed 10 during COVID for me.\par \par \uc2 FINN WORLEY (SON OF BECKY WORLEY)\par \par \uc2 Fifteen, probably.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, these are "GMA" kids, and then these are their actual classmates and friends from school, so pretty cool. We're here to learn about refurbished tech.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and refurbished tech, I actually think you guys have worked here more than me. Explain, explain for people out there, what exactly is refurbished tech?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It basically means used or secondhand. It could be a trade-in, or maybe there was a minor defect that the retailer or manufacturer was able to fix, so it's been back for checking to make sure it's okay. And an example would be Emmy has an iPhone 11 that is refurbished, purchased directly from \uc2 Apple\uc2 . Its retail price would be $549, but we got it for $80 off. It's got a new battery, a new outer shell and a warranty. You can get \uc2 Apple\uc2  care with it, too. That was a discount of $80. Finn's discount was $200 on a \uc2 Samsung\uc2  phone, normally $499, we got it for $299. So, these are really good deals. One other example, Jake here, Jake, tell these guys how old you are?\par \par \uc2 JAKE (SCHOOLCHILD)\par \par \uc2 I'm 10.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And going into what grade?\par \par \uc2 JAKE (SCHOOLCHILD)\par \par \uc2 Fifth.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fifth, so Jake's parents are not ready for him to have a smartphone, so instead they're getting him a smartwatch. It has the cell service and what have you. Now, that can be anywhere from $80 to $190 discounted from \uc2 Apple\uc2 . That's where they're purchasing these.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And for products that were already repaired and, you know, kids can be rough on stuff, throwing them in and out of bags.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh gosh. Oh man.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What are some of the products should you probably stay away from?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, yeah, the products you should stay away from, the products you should focus on, right?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You should focus on, yes, exactly.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, which are the goods, and which are the bads? So, the good ones that we really like besides phones and watches are Chromebooks. So, Chromebooks are something that kids live on right now at school. And we purchased this one from a company called Back Market. It's a really well-known company, and where you buy from is so important because they need to have warranties, they need to have return policies, and you need to know what those are. This one was $429. We got it for $365. And I'm going to tell you something, Alana here, she is one of those kids who is a torture tester. She's been through four phones already, four phones.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Four?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, we need to know\u160\'00\'A0about that warranty and that protection.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're a very expensive kid to raise, I can tell you that. Now, what should we avoid?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, what should we avoid, right. So, a couple of things to avoid, we've got Ava here and Ani, and what they have are hard drives and printers because nobody returns those for cosmetic reasons, and if there's a defect, you really don't want to be stuck with something like that. So that's a, be cautious there with the terms of those refurbished products.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Becky, great advice, saving people money, getting everybody ready to go back to school on this, this is their 41st time on the show.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220901ei830003f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR THE WORLD'S BIGGEST COUNTRY MUSIC EVENT RETURNS\b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS HELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES PRIMARY SHOWDOWNS\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, KANSAS, ABORTION, TURNOUT\par \par \uc2 PRIMARIES, RESULTS, GOP, TRUMP, CONTENTIOUS\par \par \uc2 CIPOLLONE, DOJ, SUBPOENAED, EASTMAN, PROBE\par \par \uc2 PELOSI, TAIWAN, CHINA, TENSIONS, DEMOCRACY\par \par \uc2 ALERT, STATE DEPT, AL-ZAWAHIRI, LUTE, DRONE\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, ALERT, TALIBAN, DOHA, PELOSI, CHINA\par \par \uc2 SCULLY, DODGERS, HALL OF FAME, LEGACY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT SPOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, SANCTIONS, SALAMA, KABAEVA, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 NFL, DOLPHINS, PENALIZED, BRADY, ROSS, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 CPSC\uc2 , RECALLED, T.J. MAXX, FINED, INFANT\par \par \uc2 PHILIP, PARACHUTE, TANGLED, FREEFALLING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 BASKETBALL, BLUE COLLAR U, BUFFALO\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, REFERENDUM, ELECTION, KANSAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS VOTES TO PROTECT ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTERS BLOCK AMENDMENT IN POST-ROE REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 MONKEYPOX, CHILDREN, MEDICINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING MONKEYPOX CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIFTH CHILD IN U.S. TESTS POSITIVE FOR VIRUS\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, KENTUCKY, WEATHER, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THREAT TO KENTUCKY FLOOD ZONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURVIVORS FACE DEVASTATION & DANGEROUS HEAT\par \par \uc2 LOVATO, SINGER, GENDER, IDENTITY, PRONOUNS, CRUZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMII LOVATO SPEAKS OUT ABOUT GENDER IDENTITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SINGER ADDED 'SHE/HER' PRONOUNS\par \par \uc2 DISORDERED EATING, CHILDREN, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN & DISORDERED EATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: KIDS AS YOUNG AS 9 ENGAGING IN BEHAVIOR\par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY, REFURBISHED, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO SCHOOL SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUYING REFURBISHED TECH TO CUT COSTS\par \par \uc2 STYLES, "ROAD HOUSE", NOSTALGIA\par \par \uc2 CMA, MUSIC, FESTIVAL, COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEHIND THE SCENES OF CMA FEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE WORLD'S BIGGEST COUNTRY MUSIC EVENT RETURNS\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA," live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220901ei830003j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FROM SERVICE DOG TO BEST MAN HELPING A WOUNDED VETERAN FIND HOPE AGAIN\b0\par\par\uc2 1,918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS HELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES PRIMARY SHOWDOWNS\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, KANSAS, ABORTION, TURNOUT\par \par \uc2 PRIMARIES, RESULTS, GOP, TRUMP, CONTENTIOUS\par \par \uc2 CIPOLLONE, DOJ, SUBPOENAED, EASTMAN, PROBE\par \par \uc2 PELOSI, TAIWAN, CHINA, TENSIONS, DEMOCRACY\par \par \uc2 ALERT, STATE DEPT, AL-ZAWAHIRI, LUTE, DRONE\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, ALERT, TALIBAN, DOHA, PELOSI, CHINA\par \par \uc2 SCULLY, DODGERS, HALL OF FAME, LEGACY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT SPOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, SANCTIONS, SALAMA, KABAEVA, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 NFL, DOLPHINS, PENALIZED, BRADY, ROSS, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 CPSC\uc2 , RECALLED, T.J. MAXX, FINED, INFANT\par \par \uc2 PHILIP, PARACHUTE, TANGLED, FREEFALLING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 BASKETBALL, BLUE COLLAR U, BUFFALO\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, REFERENDUM, ELECTION, KANSAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS VOTES TO PROTECT ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTERS BLOCK AMENDMENT IN POST-ROE REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 MONKEYPOX, CHILDREN, MEDICINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING MONKEYPOX CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIFTH CHILD IN U.S. TESTS POSITIVE FOR VIRUS\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, KENTUCKY, WEATHER, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THREAT TO KENTUCKY FLOOD ZONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURVIVORS FACE DEVASTATION & DANGEROUS HEAT\par \par \uc2 LOVATO, SINGER, GENDER, IDENTITY, PRONOUNS, CRUZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMII LOVATO SPEAKS OUT ABOUT GENDER IDENTITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SINGER ADDED 'SHE/HER' PRONOUNS\par \par \uc2 DISORDERED EATING, CHILDREN, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN & DISORDERED EATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: KIDS AS YOUNG AS 9 ENGAGING IN BEHAVIOR\par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY, REFURBISHED, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO SCHOOL SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUYING REFURBISHED TECH TO CUT COSTS\par \par \uc2 STYLES, "ROAD HOUSE", NOSTALGIA\par \par \uc2 CMA, MUSIC, FESTIVAL, COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEHIND THE SCENES OF CMA FEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE WORLD'S BIGGEST COUNTRY MUSIC EVENT RETURNS\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 SERVICE DOG, BEST MAN, VETERAN, MORGAN\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I accept good news for everybody. Day three of our Dog Days of Summer, and just want to highlight one of our pups from earlier in the week. Do you remember Javi, Javier?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you had Javi, yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Guess what? Javi has a new home. There's his new mom. She's going to go with the name Archie, I hear, right?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Katrina (inaudible) on Monday, she decided she wanted to adopt him. As you said, she's going to call him Archie.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations. He is a wonderful little guy, and they're all so wonderful.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They really are.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And all need great homes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know, we've got three. Oh, you've got one, oh yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I got Romeo, who's roaming now.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that's what, he won't stay on Michael's lap.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He's all over the place.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We really love teaming up with North Shore Animal League America to help these furry friends, and Romeo ran off. And so far this week, 17, we're happy to report 17 have been adopted. So if you are interested, you can scan the QR code on your screen to learn more. Michael, you're having problems over there with Romeo.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know, Romeo sees the screen behind me with dogs, and he's trying to run with those dogs back there.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know. Who let the dogs out?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This, but this week, go ahead, Romeo. Take off. We've been to Philly, Tampa and now the Dog Days of Summer is taking over Dallas, Texas. Ginger is there live outside Dallas Animal Services with a touching story. Hey, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That was good.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is so beautiful, Michael. Good luck with getting that puppy out of the studio there. But we are about to see six more dogs added to the list, and we all know, because we've got dogs at home, how much love and joy they can bring into a home and into a family. Well, for Jason Morgan it wasn't just love and joy, also some hope but a second chance at life.\par \par \uc2 JASON MORGAN (VETERAN)\par \par \uc2 There you go, come one.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Yago is a service dog, but he's been Jason's lifeline and partner for the last two years.\par \par \uc2 JASON MORGAN (VETERAN)\par \par \uc2 Good boy.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jason served as a staff sergeant combat meteorologist in the Air Force's Special Operations Unit. In 1999, Jason lost both of his legs on a mission in a remote region of Ecuador, but while his life changed forever, it was his service dog that helped him find hope once again.\par \par \uc2 JASON MORGAN (VETERAN)\par \par \uc2 I went from invisible to, like, almost like a superhero, like everyone wanted to meet my dog. In return they met me, got to know me. So really just kind of was my icebreaker back into this world.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nothing was off-limits for the veteran.\par \par \uc2 JASON MORGAN (VETERAN)\par \par \uc2 I decided that once I got my service dog, like, I'm going to get out and walk him or go somewhere and do stuff, and it just completely changed my life. Like, I ended up going to the Military Paralympics. You know, I started waterskiing, competed in snow skiing. I just, it gave me the confidence that I, I never had before.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Yago became more than Jason's service dog, even standing by his side as best man in his wedding. Yago is just one of the amazing service dogs from Canine Companions. It's an organization that provides people with more than 65 disabilities to support their independence. The pups begin in the home of one of their 1,600 volunteers.\par \par \uc2 DEVIN ORTIZ (TRAINING MANAGER)\par \par \uc2 They will teach them basic obedience, show them how to navigate the world, teach them how to learn.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After 18 months...\par \par \uc2 DOG TRAINER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Awesome, down.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...they go to one of the six campuses around the country, like here in Irving, Texas. Up to 60 dogs on this campus will go through two to three sessions a day for up to nine months before going to their forever home like Yago did for Jason.\par \par \uc2 JASON MORGAN (VETERAN)\par \par \uc2 He's my battle buddy, I call him. And so, like when I have a lot of nerve pain or something, he just rests his head, like, on my lap, like he's like, "I'm here for you, buddy."\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Canine Companions has actually placed more than 7,300 dogs since they started in 1975, and that was all because of generous donors. And we are all about generosity, aren't we here, this morning? Six dogs with their new forever families, it's about to be official, and Nilem, I wanted to talk to you because this is your first dog. Why Sunday?\par \par \uc2 NILEM (DOG OWNER)\par \par \uc2 Well, I've always wanted a dog, and when I first saw Sunday, I just fell in love with her.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, we love her, too, and we love all of them, so I say we do it. Bring out the clipboards. We have to formalize this stuff, right, so it's an exciting moment. The clipboards are being handed out. I love when the dogs get home, and they finally settle in. That's beautiful. But this has to happen first so, everybody, get their pens out and get ready to sign in three, two, one. The dog days are on. Oh, we are so happy. It is official, and I feel like this calls, because this ain't no party like a dog paw-ty, so let's bring out more dogs because there are so many dogs (inaudible) adopted, 10 represented right here. They're celebrating with their pup cups, a little whipped cream, a little sugar high, and y'all, not only the dogs you see here, but this shelter gets up to 60 dogs a day, and they really need our help, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, we have those six more dogs to add to our adopted list this week. And, Ginger, I know you are bringing a very special person at the shelter right now.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am. Yes, please, the assistant director, please come on out, Whitney Bollinger. She is making it all happen with so many volunteers here. Whitney, thank you so much. Please tell us, right now, why is this the moment to adopt dogs?\par \par \uc2 WHITNEY BOLLINGER (DALLAS ANIMAL SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 Well, any time you can adopt, it's great because you're saving a life, but right now at DAS and at shelters around the country, we are overflowing with dogs in need. And so it really is critical. It's been a very difficult summer at Dallas Animal Services, at all the shelters in our country. So, it really is time to come and save a life. Right now we're offering free adoptions. All of our pets are microchipped, they're spayed and neutered, they're vaccinated, and they're ready to be your best friend.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Whitney, we love the work that you and all the volunteers do each and every day. We know it takes a lot of love, a lot of care, time but also money. So our friends at Rachael Ray Nutrish Pet Food (inaudible) $5,000\u160\'00\'A0to help you out.\par \par \uc2 WHITNEY BOLLINGER (DALLAS ANIMAL SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 Oh my God, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, of course. I know money helps, but we need these dogs adopted, y'all.\par \par \uc2 WHITNEY BOLLINGER (DALLAS ANIMAL SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 We do.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, we do.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got that right. Ginger, thank you so much. Thank you guys in Dallas.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Get your leg over here, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All of those dogs you just saw, we want to remind you, if you're in the Dallas area, it's easy. Just check those pups out. And we've got these guys right here from North Shore Animal League America, our pals on Long Island. They are all so sweet.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Georgia has been posing a lot.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, Georgia is just a real beauty. And you guys have a QR code that you might see on your screen. If you want to hear more about the pooches and how you can adopt...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Where's Romeo?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Romeo is roaming.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wherefore art thou, Romeo?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, he had to be, he had to be contained. But yeah, anyway, you can go to the QR code to find out, and tomorrow we're in Chicago highlighting a shelter there and continuing our Dog Days of Summer.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, and yeah, Romeo is roaming. That's Romeo. Coming up, chef Alex Guarnaschelli shows us how to make a perfect summer picnic. She is here live, and we are hungry. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, we are. Yes, we are, yes, we are, yes we are.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, I like her for you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I do, too.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220901ei830003k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GR